      ],
      "id": "63a83b4d-a739-466a-9916-28edf5c77ca0",
      "name": "Resume Writer"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=ATS ANALYSIS:\n\n{{ $('Basic LLM Chain').item.json.text }}\n\n---\n\nOPTIMIZED RESUME:\n\n{{ $('Resume Writer').item.json.text }}\n\n---\n\nCreate a professional ATS Resume Optimization Report.\n\nRules:\n\n1. Extract the ATS Score from ATS Analysis.\n2. Extract all Missing Keywords.\n3. Extract all Strengths.\n4. Extract all Weaknesses.\n5. Show the complete optimized resume at the end.\n6. Do NOT show JSON.\n7. Do NOT show code blocks.\n8. Do NOT show markdown formatting.\n9. Return clean readable plain text only.\n10. Preserve line breaks in the optimized resume.\n11. Keep section headings clearly separated.\n12. Do not add explanations outside the report.\n13. If ATS Analysis contains recommendations, include them under \"RECOMMENDATIONS\".\n14. If any missing keyword has already been added to the optimized resume, mention it in recommendations.\n\nATS RESUME OPTIMIZATION REPORT\n\nATS SCORE:\n<score>\n\nMISSING KEYWORDS:\n• keyword1\n• keyword2\n• keyword3\n\nSTRENGTHS:\n• point1\n• point2\n\nWEAKNESSES:\n• point1\n• point2\n\nRECOMMENDATIONS:\n• recommendation1\n• recommendation2\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo not break sentences into multiple short lines.\n\nUse normal resume formatting.\n\nKeep paragraphs in a single line.\n\nOnly start a new line when a new section begins.\n\nOPTIMIZED RESUME\n\n<full optimized resume>",
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
